Nested Child Routes – NestJS (Notes)

1. What are Nested Child Routes?
Nested child routes allow one module to be routed inside another module
Used to create hierarchical URLs
Managed using RouterModule with children

2. Why use Nested Routes?
Better URL structure
Clear module hierarchy
Ideal for large applications

3. Basic Structure
const routes: Routes = [
  {
    path: 'parent',
    module: ParentModule,
    children: [
      {
        path: 'child',
        module: ChildModule,
      },
    ],
  },
];


4. Step-by-Step Example

Step 1: Create Modules
Admin Module (Parent)
// admin.module.ts
@Module({
  controllers: [AdminController],
})
export class AdminModule {}

// admin.controller.ts
@Controller()
export class AdminController {
  @Get('dashboard')
  dashboard() {
    return 'Admin Dashboard';
  }
}


User Module (Child)
// user.module.ts
@Module({
  controllers: [UserController],
})
export class UserModule {}

// user.controller.ts
@Controller()
export class UserController {
  @Get('list')
  listUsers() {
    return 'User List';
  }
}


Step 2: Define Nested Routes
// routes.ts
import { Routes } from '@nestjs/core';

export const routes: Routes = [
  {
    path: 'admin',
    module: AdminModule,
    children: [
      {
        path: 'users',
        module: UserModule,
      },
    ],
  },
];


Step 3: Register Routes in AppModule
// app.module.ts
@Module({
  imports: [
    AdminModule,
    UserModule,
    RouterModule.register(routes),
  ],
})
export class AppModule {}


5. Final Route URLs
URL
Controller
/admin/dashboard
AdminController
/admin/users/list
UserController


6. Important Notes
Controllers use @Controller() without prefix
Route prefixes come from RouterModule
Nesting can be multi-level

7. Multi-Level Nesting Example
/admin
  └── users
       └── roles

children: [
  {
    path: 'users',
    module: UserModule,
    children: [
      {
        path: 'roles',
        module: RoleModule,
      },
    ],
  },
];

Final URL:
/admin/users/roles


8. Key Points (Exam Ready)
Nested routes use children property
Supports deep routing hierarchy
Improves modular design
Centralized routing configuration

9. One-Line Definition
Nested child routes in NestJS allow modules to be routed inside other modules using RouterModule children for hierarchical URLs.

